I can help you design and build this app. Since you didn't specify a platform, I'll assume a **web app** (React + Node/Express + MongoDB) — but I'll keep it flexible so you can swap pieces.

Here's a complete blueprint and starter code.

---

## 1. Concept & Features

**App name idea:** "WhisperWall" / "RoastRoom" / "Echo"

**Core idea:** Users post anonymous messages. Others can react (roast, support, etc.). No names, no profiles — just vibes.

**MVP features:**
- Anonymous sign-in (device-based token, no email/password)
- Post an anonymous message (optionally target a "topic/room")
- Feed of messages
- Reactions: 👍 ❤️ 😂 🔥 (or "roast points")
- Reply anonymously (threaded)
- Report/flag a post
- Rooms/topics (e.g., #confessions, #roasts, #rants)

**Nice-to-haves:**
- "Burn" timer (post self-destructs after X hours)
- Trending posts
- Daily prompt ("Say something you'd never say out loud")
- Moderation (auto-filter profanity, manual review)

---

## 2. Tech Stack

| Layer | Choice |
|---|---|
| Frontend | React + Vite + TailwindCSS |
| Backend | Node.js + Express |
| DB | MongoDB (Mongoose) |
| Auth | Anonymous device token (UUID in localStorage) |
| Realtime | Socket.io (optional, for live feed) |
| Hosting | Vercel (front) + Render/Railway (back) + MongoDB Atlas |

